###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_53e5b1e1_6026_4ddc_8a4a_3aaaa5fdbdb7
<https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_53e5b1e1_6026_4ddc_8a4a_3aaaa5fdbdb7> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_646cdc47_f955_4da3_9398_9aac0edf48a6> ,
                                                                                     <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b3c8ba10_6bee_45e7_9416_e9019aa9f023> ,
                                                                                     [ owl:inverseOf <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b3c8ba10_6bee_45e7_9416_e9019aa9f023>
                                                                                     ] ;
                                                                  rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_1efe8b96_e006_4a33_bc9a_421406cbb9f0> ;
                                                                  rdfs:range <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_1efe8b96_e006_4a33_bc9a_421406cbb9f0> ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "hasHolisticOverlap"@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A relation between two holistic wholes that properly overlap, sharing one of their holistic parts."@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b432d2d5_25f4_4165_99c5_5935a7763c1a> """A man and the process of building a house. 
The man is a whole that possesses an holistic temporal part which is an interval of six monts and represents a working period in his lifetime.
The process of building a house is a whole that possesses an holistic spatial part which is a builder.
The working period of the man and the builder participating the building process are the same individual, belonging both to a man lifetime and to a building holistic views.
In this sense, the man and the building process overcrosses. and the overlapping individual is represented differently in both holistic views."""@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f> "This relation is about two wholes that overlap, and whose intersection is an holistic part of both."@en .


