                                                                                      ) ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Measurand"@en ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Quantity"@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc> "https://qudt.org/schema/qudt/Quantity"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A quantifiable property of a phenomenon, body, or substance."@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b432d2d5_25f4_4165_99c5_5935a7763c1a> """length
Rockwell C hardness
electric resistance"""@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_bb49844b_45d7_4f0d_8cae_8e552cbc20d6> "measurand"@en ,
                                                                                                                                    "quantity"@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f> """VIM defines a quantity as a \"property of a phenomenon, body, or substance, where the property has a magnitude that can be expressed as a number and a reference\".

A quantity in EMMO is a property and therefore only addresses the first part of the VIM definition (that is a property of a phenomenon, body, or substance). The second part (that it can be expressed as a number and a reference) is syntactic and addressed by emmo:QuantityValue."""@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_0650c031_42b6_4f0a_b62d_d88f071da6bf> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_bb49844b_45d7_4f0d_8cae_8e552cbc20d6> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "measurand"@en ;
   <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f> "VIM defines measurand as a quantity intended to be measured. This is redundant in EMMO and correspond to Quantity."@en
 ] .


