                                                                                                    )
                                                                                      ] ;
                                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_49267eba_5548_4163_8f36_518d65b583f9> ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Reductionistic"@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A class devoted to categorize causal objects by specifying their granularity levels."@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f> """A granularity level is specified by a tiling decomposition of the whole y. A tiling is identified as a set of items {x1, x2, ... xn} called tiles that:
    - are proper parts of y
    - covers the entire whole (y = x1 +x2 + ... + xn)
    - do not overlap
    - are part of one, and one only, whole (inverse functional)"""@en ,
                                                                                                                                    "Direct parthood is the antitransitive parthood relation used to build the class hierarchy (and the granularity hierarchy) for this perspective."@en .


