###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_eb3a768e_d53e_4be9_a23b_0714833c36de
<https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_eb3a768e_d53e_4be9_a23b_0714833c36de> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_802d3e92_8770_4f98_a289_ccaaab7fdddf> ;
                                                                  owl:disjointUnionOf ( <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_0f795e3e_c602_4577_9a43_d5a231aa1360>
                                                                                        <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_3f9ae00e_810c_4518_aec2_7200e424cf68>
                                                                                        <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_e7aac247_31d6_4b2e_9fd2_e842b1b7ccac>
                                                                                      ) ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Item"@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13> """A world entity is direct causally self-connected if any two parts that make up the whole are direct causally connected to each other. In the EMMO, topological connectivity is based on causality.
All physical objects, i.e. entities whose behaviour is explained by physics laws, are represented only by items. In other words, a physical object part is embedded in a direct causal graph that provides always a path between two of its parts.
Members of a collection lack such direct causality connection, i.e. they do not constitute a physical object.

Following graph theory concepts, the quantums of an item are all connected together within a network of causal relations, forming a connected causal graph. A collection is then a set of disconnected graphs."""@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84> "The disjoint union of Elementary, Quantum and CausalSystem classes."@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "The class of individuals standing for direct causally self-connected world entities."@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_eb3a768e_d53e_4be9_a23b_0714833c36de> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "Item"@en ;
   <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_705f27ae_954c_4f13_98aa_18473fc52b25> "From Latin item, \"likewise, just so, moreover\"."@en
 ] .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_eb3c61f0_3983_4346_a0c6_e7f6b90a67a8
<https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_eb3c61f0_3983_4346_a0c6_e7f6b90a67a8> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_fa3c9d4d_9fc9_4e8a_82c1_28c84e34133a> ;
