                             <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25> "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mole_%28unit%29"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                             <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84> "The mole, symbol mol, is the SI unit of amount of substance. One mole contains exactly 6.022 140 76 × 1023 elementary entities. This number is the fixed numerical value of the Avogadro constant, NA, when expressed in the unit mol−1 and is called the Avogadro number. The amount of substance, symbol n, of a system is a measure of the number of specified elementary entities. An elementary entity may be an atom, a molecule, an ion, an electron, any other particle or specified group of particles."@en ;
                             <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d> "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mole_(unit)"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                             <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_fe015383_afb3_44a6_ae86_043628697aa2> "https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.M03980" .


