                                                                                                      rdfs:comment "In experimental practice, the latter is often taken to be the moment when the rate of varia- tion of the potential of the indicator electrode attains a maximum value."@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "TransitionTime"@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "in chronopotentiometry and related techniques, the duration between the application of current and when the concentration of an electroactive substance at the electrode-solution interface becomes indistinguishable from zero"@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_fe015383_afb3_44a6_ae86_043628697aa2> "https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.T06472"@en .

